<title>JAPAN: Key June JGB futures hit all-time high of 127.04.</title>
<headline>Key June JGB futures hit all-time high of 127.04.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Key June 10-year Japanese government bond (JGB) futures rose in Tokyo on Monday afternoon to 127.04, a record high for any benchmark contract.</p>
<p>Friday's Tokyo close was 126.87.  </p>
<p>The June contract rose as high as 127.03 in London after the Tokyo session finished on Friday.</p>
<p>Steady demand for corporate straight bonds launched this afternoon, totalling about 250 billion yen, provided support for the JGB market, traders said.</p>
<p>Seven firms - NEC Corp, KDD, Sumitomo Chemical, Sumitomo Electric Industries, Sapporo Breweries, Aoki International and Chugoku Electric Power - launched straight bonds on Monday, they said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-33432-8570</p>
